<title>AUSTRALIA: CRICKET-WEST INDIES V VICTORIA 3RD DAY CLOSE.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-WEST INDIES V VICTORIA 3RD DAY CLOSE.</headline>
<dateline>WANGARATTA, Australia 1996-12-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>West Indies, needing 216 to win, were 41 for one in their second innings on the third day of their four-day cricket match against Victoria on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scores - West Indies 336 (Brian Lara 86, Sherwin Campbell 80, Jimmy Adams 52) and 41-1; Victoria 354 (Graeme Vimpani 133, Darren Berry 50; Nixon McLean 5-48) and 197.</p>
